- op: discuss  # 9206
  at: '2026-05-01T19:32:26Z'  # 9206
  by: agent  # 9206
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9206
  clock: 2  # 9206
  nonce: '9206'  # 9206
  message: "AUDIT VERDICT: DOCUMENT (with re-eval trigger). Cardinality 4 — small enough that the 'just clarify the question' fix is sufficient.\n\nFOUR LEAKAGE TESTS — UsageContext.kind: Literal['call', 'data_value', 'export', 'macro']:\n\n- Test 1 (Property derivability): 'export' is partially derivable from is_exported on Symbol (WI-zimum); 'call' is partially derivable from edge_type='calls' on the surrounding Edge. The duplication is small but real. **LIGHT LEAKAGE.**\n- Test 2 (Apex/peer): No value is used as both 'top type' and 'peer subtype'. **PASSES.**\n- Test 3 (Construct vs relationship): 'call' is a syntactic construct (function-call expression); 'macro' is a syntactic construct (macro invocation expression); 'export' is a relationship (this thing is publicly visible); 'data_value' is a semantic role (this thing carries data). **THREE QUESTION-CATEGORIES competing in 4 values. FIRES.**\n- Test 4 (Mechanism vs category): 'call'/'macro' are mechanisms (HOW the symbol is referenced); 'data_value'/'export' are categories (WHAT the reference means). **LIGHT FIRE.**\n\nTHE CONFUSION, NAMED: the field doesn't have a single coherent question. It mixes 'how is the symbol invoked?' (call/macro) with 'what is this reference for?' (data_value/export).\n\nVERDICT — DOCUMENT, NOT DEPRECATE-NOW:\n\nCardinality is small (4). The runtime impact is bounded — UsageContext is a relatively narrow IR concept used for framework-pattern detection (route handlers, decorators, etc.), not a wide-blast-radius enum. Splitting into orthogonal fields (e.g., usage_construct ∈ {call, macro} + usage_role ∈ {data_value, export}) would require migrating every UsageContext producer + every consumer that filters on .kind.\n\nThe lighter alternative is a docstring clarification that names the question this field actually answers and the boundary at which it would warrant a split.\n\nDOCUMENT NOW: at the field declaration in ir.py UsageContext, add a docstring section: 'kind names how the surrounding source code references this symbol — either as a syntactic construct (call, macro) or as a semantic role (data_value, export). The field currently mixes axes; future values that don't fit either question should trigger a split into separate construct/role fields. See WI-gatuh-ruvar audit verdict.'\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS:\n1. A FIFTH value is proposed that doesn't fit either the construct axis or the semantic-role axis — that's the moment to split.\n2. A consumer needs to filter by 'all-construct-shapes' or 'all-semantic-role-shapes' independently — today no consumer needs this; the field's downstream use is the framework-pattern detector picking specific values for specific patterns.\n3. A bug surfaces where 'export' classification was wrong because the consumer needed both 'is this exported?' AND 'is this called?' separately — that's the failure mode the split would prevent.\n\nFOLLOW-UP: filing WI-(new) for the docstring update at UsageContext.kind in ir.py. Lowest-priority of the four audit follow-ups (P4 already, just docstring)."  # 9206
